{"name":"Fashion District","hex":"#b9a998","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fashion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A current (constantly changing) trend, favored for frivolous rather than practical, logical, or intellectual reasons.","Popular trends, especially in clothing; the industry that designs clothing and sometimes other related items."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make, build or construct, especially in a crude or improvised way.","To make in a standard manner; to work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashion"},{"term":"district","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An administrative division of an area.","An area or region marked by some distinguishing feature."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To divide into administrative or other districts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/district"}],"entries":[{"title":"Los Angeles Fashion District","blocks":[{"text":"The Los Angeles Fashion District, previously known as the Garment District, is a business improvement district (BID) in, and often cited as a sub-neighborhood of, downtown Los Angeles. The neighborhood caters to wholesale selling and has more than 4,000 overwhelmingly independently owned and operated retail and wholesale businesses selling apparel, footwear, accessories, and fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Men%27s_Accessory_Wholesaler%2C_Fashion_District%2C_Pico_%26_Santee%2C_Los_Angeles.JPG/330px-Men%27s_Accessory_Wholesaler%2C_Fashion_District%2C_Pico_%26_Santee%2C_Los_Angeles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Fashion_District"},{"title":"Fashion District, Toronto","blocks":[{"text":"The Fashion District is a commercial and residential district in Downtown Toronto, Ontario, Canada. It is located between the intersection of Bathurst Street to the west, Spadina Avenue to the east, Queen Street West to the north and Front Street to the south. Google Maps extends the district further east of Spadina Avenue to Peter Street."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Fashion_District_Artwork.JPG/330px-Fashion_District_Artwork.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fashion_District%2C_Toronto"},{"title":"Fashion","blocks":[{"text":"Fashion is a term used interchangeably to describe the creation of clothing, footwear, accessories, cosmetics, and jewellery of different cultural aesthetics and their mix and match into outfits that depict distinctive ways of dressing as signifiers of social status, self-expression, and group belonging. As a multifaceted term, fashion describes an industry, designs, aesthetics, and trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg/330px-Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fashion"},{"title":"District","blocks":[{"text":"A district is a type of administrative division that in some countries is managed by the local government. Across the world, areas known as \"districts\" vary greatly in size, spanning regions or counties, several municipalities, subdivisions of municipalities, school district, or political district."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/District"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg/500px-Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg/1280px-Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg/500px-Santee_Alley_LA_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi